      "Merged the critic's candidate rules into surface-level segmentation guidance: do not treat the first-conjunct cut, verb-complement cuts, auxiliary+oblique splits, 'As <TITLE>' role splits, and contrastive/limiter splits as high-confidence — instead rank them low (or lowest) so they survive candidacy but are chosen last by the deterministic truncator. Rationale: these patterns caused wrong-participant, head-not-yet-arrived and scope errors; demoting them preserves options while preventing premature commits.",
