    "changelog": [
      "Merged the critic's candidate rules into surface-level segmentation guidance: do not treat the first-conjunct cut, verb-complement cuts, auxiliary+oblique splits, 'As <TITLE>' role splits, and contrastive/limiter splits as high-confidence — instead rank them low (or lowest) so they survive candidacy but are chosen last by the deterministic truncator. Rationale: these patterns caused wrong-participant, head-not-yet-arrived and scope errors; demoting them preserves options while preventing premature commits.",
      "Expanded the 'main clause / coordinating conjunction' and 'after finite verbs' guidance in [When to Segment] to explicitly detect the 4-token and 3-token lookahead windows demanded by the measured failure cases, so the rule is decidable from the source surface form.",
      "Added explicit ranking instructions in [Priority Rules] and precise handling in [Decision Procedure] to ensure candidates matching these risky patterns are assigned the lowest confidence ranks during the ranking pass rather than being absolutely forbidden during candidacy."
    ],
    "next_changelog": [
      "Clarified core principle: prefer promoting safe, high-confidence boundaries rather than broadly demoting risky ones; rank adjustments should be narrow, local, and use short lookahead.",
      "Made candidacy rules explicitly generous and surface-only; moved all lookahead checks into the ranking pass and limited them to 2–3 tokens to avoid over-demotion.",
      "Added positive promotion signals: explicit conditions that raise a candidate to top rank when a clause is clearly complete and no short complement/subordinator follows.",
      "Replaced blanket low/high demotions with targeted, lightweight ranking downgrades for specific risky surface patterns (verb+complement, 'between/among' participant lists, 'As TITLE' preposed roles, passive 'by' obliques, contrastive limiters), only when those patterns appear within a short lookahead window."
    ]
